{
  "scenario_id": "sim-aidc-chiller-cascade-and-standby",
  "title": "AIDC: lone-chiller cascade and pump-pair degradation",
  "description": "A lone chiller (N, no partner) serves a chilled-water loop whose dual pumps (N+1) shield row cooling in the assessor's single-fault view. When the chiller actually dies, the water service dies with it, both pumps lose their supply, and the pump pair cannot save row cooling — the cascade exceeds the what-if label (cooling and IT fall with the water loop). The repair restores every cascade-dead node at once. Then one pump faults (absorbed; the surviving pump becomes a new single point of failure — degraded tolerance made visible in the SPOF list), the second pump faults (cooling and IT fall, the water loop survives), and one repair restores the service. Adjudicates Category 2's central case: secondary losses flowing through a protecting group's own supply.",
  "market": "aidc",
  "facility_id": "sim-aidc-chiller-cascade",
